## Slide Accessibility Note
- **Images:** none; diagrams are HTML text with labels.
- **Speaker Notes:** These slides follow the Module 06 follow-along script
  and the book chapter Your Project Repository. The live coding happens in
  `class/week_06_follow_along.R`.

## Today: Two Halves

::: {.diagram-flow .diagram-compact aria-label="Today's workflow: read the wide table, ask what each column means, pivot_longer to tidy, summarize, pivot_wider to show. Then, after the break, create your project repository"}
<div class="diagram-node">Read the wide table</div>
<div class="diagram-arrow" aria-hidden="true">-&gt;</div>
<div class="diagram-node">Ask what each column means</div>
<div class="diagram-arrow" aria-hidden="true">-&gt;</div>
<div class="diagram-node"><code>pivot_longer()</code></div>
<div class="diagram-arrow" aria-hidden="true">-&gt;</div>
<div class="diagram-node">Summarize</div>
<div class="diagram-arrow" aria-hidden="true">-&gt;</div>
<div class="diagram-node"><code>pivot_wider()</code></div>
:::

<p class="diagram-caption">After the break: your semester project repository.</p>

- **No Assignment 06.** Your project proposal is the work for the next two
  weeks (**due Sun Nov 15**).
- **Mon Nov 2: no class meeting.** You do the project data audit on your
  own.

## Get Today's Files: Pull

I added two files to your **Module 05** repo on GitHub:
`class/week_06_follow_along.R` and `class/data/drought.csv`.

:::: {.columns}
::: {.column width="50%"}
**GitHub Desktop**

1. Commit anything changed
2. **Fetch origin**
3. **Pull origin**
:::
::: {.column width="50%"}
**Positron**

1. Once, in the Terminal:<br>`git config --global pull.rebase false`
2. Source Control: commit anything changed
3. **...** menu > **Pull**
:::
